    "title": "Surveillance video leads to arrest in theft from Foley business - NewsBreak",
    "text": "FOLEY, Ala. ( WKRG ) — Foley Police used surveillance video to identify a suspect in a theft at a Foley business. According to a Foley Police Department news release, at about 7:30 a.m. June 9, officers responded to Sweat Tire on County Road 12 after an employee called about damage to the building and cars broken into. When police arrived, they saw cars and equipment had been burned, other cars “had clearly been rummaged through” and learned of several stolen items, including a pickup truck, the release said. 42-year-old Daniel Kelso of Foley was arrested on June 14 after FPD detectives used surveillance footage and other investigative techniques. Kelso is charged with two counts of unlawful breaking and entering a motor vehicle, and one count of first-degree theft of property the release said. These felonies can lead to more than 2 years in prison and charges up to 30 thousand dollars. City officials say the stolen vehicle was recovered in Mobile with help from the Mobile Police Department For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
